{"type":"text","timestamp":1794349689275,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c79368e7001G3X7ikkqvC149w","messageID":"msg_1c7934e87001LxMyF60dktTGZS","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"text","text":"<think>Let me look at the existing app.py, App.tsx, main.tsx, and check git status.\n\nLet me plan the work:\n\nBackend (Flask):\n- SQLite under ./data\n- Auth: register/login with token (use secrets.token_hex or itsdangerous signed tokens). No extra dependencies needed — use `hashlib` for password hashing (pbkdf2) and `secrets` for tokens.\n- Items CRUD, movements, pagination, filters.\n- Serve frontend build from frontend/dist.\n\nFrontend (React + TS + Vite + Tailwind):\n- Need Tailwind CSS. Tailwind v4 with @tailwindcss/vite plugin, or v3 with postcss. The sandbox has network access to public package registries, so I can npm install tailwindcss. But there's package-lock.json — need to update it. Let me check network availability.\n\nLet me check what's available.\n\nLet me read the existing files first.","time":{"start":1794349689063,"end":1794349689229}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794349689275,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call-1412bb71-440b-4596-89e1-456211ffc862","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py"},"output":"<path>/workspace/backend/app.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"Flask entry point.\"\"\"\n2: \n3: from pathlib import Path\n4: \n5: from flask import Flask\n6: from flask import send_from_directory\n7: \n8: DIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n9: \n10: app = Flask(__name__, static_folder=None)\n11: \n12: \n13: @app.get(\"/api/health\")\n14: def health():\n15:     return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n16: \n17: \n18: @app.get(\"/\")\n19: @app.get(\"/<path:path>\")\n20: def frontend(path: str = \"index.html\"):\n21:     if (DIST / path).is_file():\n22:         return send_from_directory(DIST, path)\n23:     return send_from_directory(DIST, \"index.html\")\n\n(End of file - total 23 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"Flask entry point.\"\"\"\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom flask import Flask\nfrom flask import send_from_directory\n\nDIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n\napp = Flask(__name__, static_folder=None)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/api/health\")\ndef health():\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\n@app.get(\"/<path:path>\")\ndef frontend(path: str = \"index.html\"):","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/backend/app.py","text":"\"\"\"Flask entry point.\"\"\"\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom flask import Flask\nfrom flask import send_from_directory\n\nDIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n\napp = Flask(__name__, static_folder=None)\n\n\n@app.get(\"/api/health\")\ndef health():\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\n@app.get(\"/<path:path>\")\ndef frontend(path: str = \"index.html\"):\n    if (DIST / path).is_file():\n        return send_from_directory(DIST, path)\n    return send_from_directory(DIST, \"index.html\")","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":23,"totalLines":23,"truncated":false}},"title":"backend/app.py","time":{"start":1794349689089,"end":1794349689261}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c79368f1001pSpfO7ljAGVt5S","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","messageID":"msg_1c7934e87001LxMyF60dktTGZS"}}
