{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794350406107,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c79e59bc001zQ4HQgfZ88z5q3","messageID":"msg_1c79e129e001r2xAf7gcR6jM8g","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794350406108,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c79e59bf001HvMDdOvN3AQ8WT","messageID":"msg_1c79e129e001r2xAf7gcR6jM8g","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"text","text":"<think>Vitest 3.2.7 and @testing-library/react 16.3.3 installed. Note esbuild postinstall was skipped (\"install-scripts\" warning) — vitest 3 uses esbuild? It uses vite → esbuild. If the esbuild binary wasn't installed, vitest may fail. Let me check by running a trivial test.\n\nActually the warning says npm skipped install scripts (probably due to a sandbox policy). esbuild's postinstall downloads/links the platform binary — with npm optional deps, `@esbuild/linux-x64` package provides the binary directly; the postinstall just validates. Let me test.\n\nLet me create the vitest config and a test file.\n\nvitest.config.ts:\n```ts\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport tailwindcss from \"@tailwindcss/vite\";\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n  test: {\n    environment: \"jsdom\",\n    globals: true,\n    setupFiles: [\"./src/test/setup.ts\"],\n    include: [\"src/**/*.test.tsx\"],\n  },\n});\n```\nHmm, but vite.config.ts already exists with plugins; vitest reads vite.config.ts by default. I can add a `test` key to vite.config.ts but that requires importing \"vitest/config\" types. Simpler: create vitest.config.ts which overrides vite.config.ts (vitest prefers vitest.config.ts). Let me create vitest.config.ts.\n\nsetup.ts: polyfill for window.matchMedia? Not used. localStorage exists in jsdom. fetch: jsdom in Node 22+ has global fetch? Vitest's jsdom environment provides fetch from Node (undici). Node 24 has fetch globally. But jsdom environment may not expose fetch... Vitest jsdom env copies jsdom window properties; `fetch` is not in jsdom, but Vitest adds Node's fetch? In Vitest, `environment: 'jsdom'` keeps globalThis.fetch from Node (I believe Vitest's jsdom env populates globals from jsdom window but keeps some Node globals like fetch). To be safe, in setup I'll explicitly set globalThis.fetch to Node's fetch with a base URL prefix.\n\nSetup:\n```ts\nconst base = process.env.API_BASE_URL ?? \"http://127.0.0.1:8123\";\nconst originalFetch = globalThis.fetch;\nglobalThis.fetch = ((input: RequestInfo | URL, init?: RequestInit) => {\n  const url = typeof input === \"string\" ? new URL(input, base).toString() : input instanceof URL ? new URL(input, base).toString() : input;\n  return originalFetch(url as any, init);\n}) as typeof fetch;\n```\nCareful: `input` could be a Request object; fine for our usage (all string URLs).\n\nAlso `window.scrollTo` is not implemented in jsdom → it logs \"Not implemented\" errors. My code calls window.scrollTo(0,0) in navigate and scrollIntoView (jsdom doesn't implement scrollIntoView → TypeError!). jsdom doesn't implement Element.prototype.scrollIntoView → calling it throws \"TypeError: element.scrollIntoView is not a function\". I need to stub it in setup:\n```ts\nElement.prototype.scrollIntoView = () => {};\nwindow.scrollTo = () => {};\n```\nAlso `PopStateEvent` exists in jsdom. Fine.\n\nNow the test file. Let me write an integration test against the live Flask server.\n\nTest plan:\n```tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeAll, afterEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen, waitFor, within } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport userEvent from \"@testing-library/user-event\";\nimport App from \"../App\";\n```\nNeed @testing-library/user-event — install it.\n\nTest 1: render App → expect \"Warehouse Inventory\" heading, \"Sign in\" form visible.\nTest 2: register → header shows \"Signed in as testuser\".\nTest 3: add item → table row appears.\nTest 4: low stock switch → filters.\nTest 5: click item → item page → receive stock → quantity updates.\nTest 6: delete → confirm modal → item removed.\n\nAlso need localStorage cleared between tests, and the DB cleaned between tests (use unique usernames/SKUs per test to avoid conflicts).\n\nLet me install @testing-library/user-event and write the tests.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794350406079,"end":1794350406104}}}
