{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794350415191,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call-eb053bbb-85d1-4b36-9b1a-f571d3527583","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"const baseUrl = process.env.API_BASE_URL ?? \"http://127.0.0.1:8123\";\nconst originalFetch = globalThis.fetch;\n\nglobalThis.fetch = ((input: RequestInfo | URL, init?: RequestInit) => {\n  const target =\n    typeof input === \"string\"\n      ? new URL(input, baseUrl).toString()\n      : input instanceof URL\n        ? new URL(input, baseUrl).toString()\n        : input;\n  return originalFetch(target as RequestInfo, init);\n}) as typeof fetch;\n\nElement.prototype.scrollIntoView = function scrollIntoView() {\n  return;\n};\n\nwindow.scrollTo = (() => {\n  return;\n}) as typeof window.scrollTo;\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/test/setup.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/test/setup.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/test/setup.ts","time":{"start":1794350415168,"end":1794350415175}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c79e7d3a0019M7auF800z8UOL","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","messageID":"msg_1c79e705b001xeeGXsVvZKtJHp"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794350415192,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c79e7d49001l0wYX883Z6WGRa","reason":"tool-calls","messageID":"msg_1c79e705b001xeeGXsVvZKtJHp","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":68661,"input":120,"output":189,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":68352}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794350448564,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c79effa6001KEdnk2XDZnOlzk","messageID":"msg_1c79e7d53001L5q4P0w0ZJTW8E","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794350448565,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c79effa80018tIKL2YY5sPcuy","messageID":"msg_1c79e7d53001L5q4P0w0ZJTW8E","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"text","text":"<think>Now the test file. Let me write an integration test.\n\n```tsx\nimport { afterEach, beforeAll, describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\nimport { cleanup, render, screen, waitFor, within } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport userEvent from \"@testing-library/user-event\";\nimport App from \"../App\";\n\nfunction unique(prefix: string) {\n  return `${prefix}-${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8)}`;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"inventory app\", () => {\n  afterEach(() => {\n    cleanup();\n    window.localStorage.clear();\n  });\n\n  it(\"shows the inventory table to anonymous visitors\", async () => {\n    render(<App />);\n    expect(await screen.findByRole(\"heading\", { name: \"Inventory\" })).toBeTruthy();\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: /sign in/i })).toBeTruthy();\n  });\n\n  it(\"registers a user and signs them in\", async () => {\n    const user = userEvent.setup();\n    render(<App />);\n    const username = unique(\"user\");\n    await user.type(await screen.findByLabelText(\"New username\"), username);\n    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(\"New password\"), \"secret123\");\n    await user.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Register\" }));\n    expect(await screen.findByText(username)).toBeTruthy();\n  });\n  ...\n```\n\nCareful with `getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Register\" })` — there's only one. And \"Sign in\" button appears in the header AND in the auth panel (submit). Ambiguity! `getByRole(\"button\", {name: \"Sign in\"})` would match both the header button and the form submit button → strict mode error. Use `getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Sign in\", exact: false })`... still ambiguous. I'll use `within(screen.getByRole(\"form\", { name: \"Sign in\" }))`. Note: a <form> with aria-label has role \"form\". I set aria-label on the forms: `aria-label=\"Sign in\"` and `aria-label=\"Register\"`. Good.\n\nHmm, but the header \"Sign in\" button and the panel's submit \"Sign in\" — with getAllByRole it's fine.\n\nLet me write the tests using `within(form)`.\n\nFor the item page flow: click on the item link (text = item name) → ItemPage renders.\n\nNote the ItemPage has an \"Item not found\" if item deleted.\n\nAlso note: after registering, the AuthPanel disappears (username set) → the header shows \"Signed in as X\".\n\nTest: add item:\n```tsx\nawait user.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Add item\" }));\nconst dialog = await screen.findByRole(\"dialog\");\nawait user.type(within(dialog).getByLabelText(\"Name\"), \"Widget\");\nawait user.type(within(dialog).getByLabelText(\"SKU\"), sku);\nawait user.type(within(dialog).getByLabelText(\"Location\"), \"Aisle 1\");\nawait user.clear(within(dialog).getByLabelText(\"Opening quantity\"));\nawait user.type(within(dialog).getByLabelText(\"Opening quantity\"), \"5\");\nawait user.clear(within(dialog).getByLabelText(\"Reorder level\"));\nawait user.type(within(dialog).getByLabelText(\"Reorder level\"), \"3\");\nawait user.click(within(dialog).getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Create item\" }));\nexpect(await screen.findByText(\"Widget\")).toBeTruthy();\n```\n\nDuplicate sku test: add same sku again → expect error text \"already exists\".\n\nReceive flow:\n```tsx\nawait user.click(screen.getByText(\"Widget\"));  // link\nexpect(await screen.findByRole(\"heading\", { name: \"Widget\" })).toBeTruthy();\nconst receiveForm = screen.getByRole(\"form\", { name: \"Receive\" });\nawait user.type(within(receiveForm).getByLabelText(\"Amount\"), \"7\");\nawait user.click(within(receiveForm).getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Receive stock\" }));\n// quantity updates to 12\nawait waitFor(() => expect(screen.getByText(\"12\")).toBeTruthy());\n```\nHmm, \"12\" may appear in multiple places (quantity_after in movements table). Use a more specific query: the big quantity display. Let me add a data-testid? Instead, query the h1's sibling. Simpler: check the movement history contains \"+7\" and the item page shows quantity via `screen.getByText(\"12\")` — ambiguous.\n\nI'll add a `data-testid=\"item-quantity\"` to the quantity display in ItemPage to make the test robust. That's a small addition to production code, acceptable.\n\nLow stock test: item with quantity 5, reorder level 3 → not low. After receiving? Let me create an item with quantity 2 and reorder level 5 → low stock → the row has \"Low stock\" badge and the row has bg-amber class. Test: create item with qty 2, reorder 5 → table shows \"Low stock\" badge; toggle the switch → the item is still visible; add another item not low → after toggling it's hidden.\n\nSimpler assertions: with low_stock=true, the API returns only low-stock items. I'll test the UI: create \"LowOne\" (qty 1, reorder 5) and \"HighOne\" (qty 20, reorder 5); toggle switch → expect \"LowOne\" visible and \"HighOne\" not in the document.\n\nPaging test: create 3 items with page size 10 → not needed. Skip paging test or set page size 10 and create 12 items — slow. I'll test paging via API already covered. Let me include a light paging test: set \"Per page\" to 10 and create 11 items → \"Page 1 of 2\" and Next enabled. Creating 11 items via UI is slow (each is a dialog). Instead, create items via the API directly in the test (fetch) and then check the table. That's fast. Good idea: use fetch directly for seeding.\n\nDelete test: on item page click \"Delete item\" → confirm dialog appears → click \"Delete\" → back on inventory → item gone.\n\nLet me write the test file now.\n\nOne concern: `screen.getByText(\"Widget\")` might match multiple (item name in table + movement?). On the inventory page, the item name appears once. Fine.\n\nAnother concern: the header \"Sign in\" link/button vs the AuthPanel \"Sign in\" heading (h2) — different roles, fine.\n\nLet me write it.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794350448552,"end":1794350448562}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794350448588,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-ecbc35db-a70f-408b-8a3f-80f4d8e16982","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx","newString":"          <div className=\"text-right\">\n            <p className=\"text-3xl font-bold tabular-nums text-slate-900\" data-testid=\"item-quantity\">\n              {item.quantity}\n            </p>\n            <p className=\"text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500\">In stock</p>\n          </div>","oldString":"          <div className=\"text-right\">\n            <p className=\"text-3xl font-bold tabular-nums text-slate-900\">{item.quantity}</p>\n            <p className=\"text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500\">In stock</p>\n          </div>","replaceAll":false},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx\n@@ -351,9 +351,11 @@\n       {item.location ? ` · ${item.location}` : \"\"}\n     </p>\n   </div>\n   <div className=\"text-right\">\n-    <p className=\"text-3xl font-bold tabular-nums text-slate-900\">{item.quantity}</p>\n+    <p className=\"text-3xl font-bold tabular-nums text-slate-900\" data-testid=\"item-quantity\">\n+      {item.quantity}\n+    </p>\n     <p className=\"text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500\">In stock</p>\n   </div>\n </div>\n <div className=\"mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm\">\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx\n@@ -351,9 +351,11 @@\n       {item.location ? ` · ${item.location}` : \"\"}\n     </p>\n   </div>\n   <div className=\"text-right\">\n-    <p className=\"text-3xl font-bold tabular-nums text-slate-900\">{item.quantity}</p>\n+    <p className=\"text-3xl font-bold tabular-nums text-slate-900\" data-testid=\"item-quantity\">\n+      {item.quantity}\n+    </p>\n     <p className=\"text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500\">In stock</p>\n   </div>\n </div>\n <div className=\"mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm\">\n","additions":3,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/pages/ItemPage.tsx","time":{"start":1794350448559,"end":1794350448572}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c79effaa001tROSJvq08qkNj9","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","messageID":"msg_1c79e7d53001L5q4P0w0ZJTW8E"}}
