{"type":"text","timestamp":1794350502674,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c79fd2fd001rDVK9Dmlhi4j2d","messageID":"msg_1c79fa00f001zVNJsydMTgG2ZA","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"text","text":"<think>Good progress. Test failures:\n1. \"adds an item and rejects a duplicate sku\": multiple elements match /already exists/i — the banner and the field error both show it. Fix the test to use findAllByText. That's a test issue, not app. But it also suggests showing the same message twice is redundant — fine, but let me keep both (banner + field) since tests might look for either. I'll update the test to use `findAllByText`.\n\n2. The \"records movements on the item page\" test failed at line 161: `await user.click(await screen.findByText(name));` — it found multiple? The error shows \"Found multiple elements\" maybe. Let me look at the other failures in detail. Actually the output at line 161 error was \"Unable to find an element with the text\" or multiple? The tail showed a DOM dump; the error line points to 161. Let me re-run and see the specific failures for tests 3-6.\n\nLet me get a summary of each failure.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794350502653,"end":1794350502670}}}
