{"type":"text","timestamp":1794350543013,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c7a07095001CxNRLDgAiAGJoa","messageID":"msg_1c7a031cd001zrqdZgYtJctmHw","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"text","text":"<think>\"Found multiple elements with the text: Widget\" — the item name appears twice: once in the table and once in the \"4 items tracked\" text? No... \"Widget\" appears in the table cell and possibly in the dialog (still open?) or in the notice. Wait, the first test: after creating the item, the dialog closes. The table has the name. Where's the second \"Widget\"? Possibly the \"Add item\" dialog's input still holds the value (input value \"Widget\" — but getByText doesn't match input values). Hmm.\n\nAh — maybe the table renders the item name in the link, and the second occurrence is in... the \"Showing X of Y items\"? No.\n\nWait, in the duplicate test, the first creation succeeded and the dialog closed; then \"Widget\" appears in the table. But the failure says multiple elements with text \"Widget\" — the second is \"Widget copy\"? No, that contains \"Widget\" as a substring! getByText matches substring? No — getByText with a string matches the full normalized text content by default (exact match on the element's text). \"Widget copy\" != \"Widget\". Hmm, but \"Found multiple elements with the text: Widget\" occurred at the line `expect(await screen.findByText(\"Widget\")).toBeTruthy();`.\n\nWait, maybe the item name appears both in the table link AND in the input? No.\n\nHold on: the second failure in the low stock test says \"Unable to find an element with the text: Low-aeb9ws\" — the item was created but not found in the table. That suggests the items list didn't refresh after creating an item! In the first test, \"Widget\" was found multiple times... Hmm, maybe the table didn't update and instead the *dialog* still contained \"Widget\" as text? No, dialog inputs.\n\nLet me think again about `onCreated` in ItemDialog: it calls `onCreated(item)` then `onClose()`. In InventoryPage, `onCreated` sets page 1, reloads locations, clears notice. But it does NOT refresh the items list! The list refresh happens only via the filter effect (which doesn't re-run). So the new item doesn't appear in the table — that's the bug (\"Unable to find ... Low-aeb9ws\").\n\nSo why did the first test find \"Widget\" multiple times? Because the item name \"Widget\" appears in the DOM... where? Possibly in the `<title>`? No. Hmm, maybe the table did refresh? No...\n\nAh wait — the \"Showing 4 of 4 items\" text and... no.\n\nLet me debug by rendering the DOM. Actually: in the first test, after creating the item with name \"Widget\", the findByText(\"Widget\") found multiple elements. Since the table doesn't refresh, where do \"Widget\" texts come from? The ItemDialog is closed (unmounted). Unless... the dialog isn't closing because `onClose` is called but `open` state... `setAddOpen(false)` — yes it's called.\n\nHmm, but maybe the table DID update in the first test (because the \"Add item\" dialog's `useEffect` on [open] resets fields...). No.\n\nWait — maybe the effect that fetches items re-ran because `pageSize`/`page` changed? `onCreated` calls `setPage(1)` — page was already 1, so no state change → no re-fetch.\n\nHmm, so how did \"Widget\" get into the DOM twice? Let me actually debug this. Maybe the AuthPanel \"Sign in\"/\"Register\" forms... no.\n\nLet me write a quick debug test to dump the DOM after creating an item.\n\nActually — I bet the two elements are the table cell link and... the `<td>`? No, getByText matches the closest element whose text matches; if both a `<td>` and `<a>` contain exactly \"Widget\", both match! Indeed: the `<td>` contains the `<a>` with text \"Widget\" — the td's textContent is \"Widget\" too, so both the td and the a match → \"multiple elements\". That's the classic nested-element issue. In the first test, \"Widget\" appeared in a td (with a link) → 2 matches. And in the other tests, the item never got into the table → 0 matches.\n\nFix the app: refresh the items list after create/delete. I'll add a `reload` trigger state (e.g., `reloadKey`) to the fetch effect.\n\nAlso to reduce ambiguity for tests, I could make the name cell contain only the link (the td contains only the link, so nested match still occurs). Any test doing getByText(\"Widget\") on a table would hit this. Playwright's getByText also matches multiple? Playwright's `getByText` matches the smallest element? Playwright text engine matches elements whose text content matches, and it does match both parent and child? In Playwright, `page.getByText('Widget')` may match multiple elements too (it matches the deepest elements? Actually Playwright's text selector matches \"the smallest element containing specified text\" — Playwright docs: \"Matching always normalizes whitespace... Input elements of the type button and submit are matched by their value instead of text content.\" And for `text=` engine: \"matches the smallest element containing specified text\"). So Playwright matches only the smallest element → td > a → the a is the smallest → single match. Good, Playwright is fine.\n\nTesting Library's getByText matches all elements whose text content matches (including ancestors) → ambiguity. I'll adjust my tests to use `getAllByText` or scope to the link role.\n\nSo:\n1. Fix the app to reload items after create/delete (real bug).\n2. Adjust tests to use more specific queries (e.g., `screen.findByRole(\"link\", { name })`).\n\nAlso I should double check the item page: clicking the link (role link) works.\n\nLet me fix InventoryPage: add `const [reloadToken, setReloadToken] = useState(0);` and include it in the fetch effect deps; `onCreated` → `setReloadToken((v) => v + 1)`.\n\nAlso after deleting an item, the inventory list should refresh — deletion happens on the ItemPage and navigates to \"/\" — the InventoryPage remounts (route change) → fresh fetch. Fine.\n\nLet me apply the fix.</think>\n\nFound a real bug (list didn't refresh after creating an item). Fixing it:","time":{"start":1794350542997,"end":1794350543009}}}
