{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794350582469,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c7a10aad001rG1awvxCyjBVi3","messageID":"msg_1c7a0ee48001GsWHVesT93pBv6","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794350582469,"sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","part":{"id":"prt_1c7a10ab0001Zvb5KPBV24b7IF","messageID":"msg_1c7a0ee48001GsWHVesT93pBv6","sessionID":"ses_e386cd387ffeGJ3KEnYGDpYp5r","type":"text","text":"<think>Progress. Now:\n\n1. \"Found multiple elements with the role link and name Widget\" — because the previous test data persists in the shared DB? No wait, \"Widget\" is the exact name I used in the duplicate test (not unique). Earlier tests created \"Widget\" items in the same DB (the DB persists across test runs!). The DB isn't cleaned between tests, so multiple \"Widget\" items exist from previous runs. I should use unique names in the test (e.g., `unique(\"Widget\")`).\n\n2. \"records movements on the item page\": the item name is unique (\"Widget-d645ve\") but not found → because after creating the item, the list refresh happens via reloadToken → but the item's name link is a link with role link... it should be there. Hmm, \"Unable to find role=link and name Widget-58dg0p\".\n\nWait — maybe the issue is that after creating the item, `setPage(1)` + reloadToken triggers a fetch; the table shows the item. But the test does `await screen.findByRole(\"link\", { name })` immediately after clicking \"Create item\" — findByRole waits up to 1000ms. Should be enough.\n\nHmm, unless the item wasn't created: in that test I typed Name and SKU, cleared quantity and typed \"5\"... `user.clear()` on a number input then type \"5\" → value \"5\". Fine.\n\nBut wait: the SKU is unique() so no conflict. Hmm.\n\nOh! I see a potential issue: `user.clear()` requires the element to be editable; fine.\n\nLet me check whether the item was created by looking at the failing DOM output. Let me run just that test with more output.\n\nActually — maybe the problem is that the ItemDialog's `useEffect` on [open] resets the form fields when `open` changes... it resets when the dialog opens (true). Fine.\n\nAnother thought: after creating the item, `onCreated` → `setPage(1)`, `setReloadToken` → re-fetch → items list includes the new item. The link's accessible name is the item name. Should be found.\n\nUnless... the fetch effect's cleanup cancels the promise and `items` isn't updated? With StrictMode in dev? Vitest renders <App /> which includes StrictMode → effects run twice in React 19 StrictMode (mount, unmount, remount). The cleanup sets cancelled = true for the first run, then the second run fetches again → fine.\n\nLet me debug by running that single test and dumping the DOM.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794350582448,"end":1794350582466}}}
